{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>מי אנכי</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one and the other מי אנכי הביאותני עד הלום, in the passage of David. Teaches that Moses sought kingship for himself and for his descendants, but the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to give it to him, as stated: אל תקרב הלום, and הלום is none other than kingship. Moses said: Since the kingship ceases from me and is not for my children — שלח נא ביד תשלח."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Masoretic parallel is 2 Samuel 7:18. The citation אל תקרב הלום is from Exodus 3:5; the argument links the word הלום across both verses. The phrase ואינו לבני is translated hyper-literally; possibly should read ואינה לבני."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:47.231795112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}